---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code as CodeSnippet } from "astro:components";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/foce/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Section Summary: Control Flow</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-4" />

        <p class="text-secondary">
          Activities 1.10 &ndash; 1.17. Use this to review, or to fill in a
          definition you missed.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">1.</span> Booleans and Conditions</h2>

          <p>
            A comparison produces a boolean, and an{" "}
            <CodeSnippet
              code="if"
              lang={"python"}
              theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
              inline
            /> statement uses that boolean to decide whether to run a block. In Python,
            indentation is what marks the block.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Boolean</dt>
            <dd>
              A value that is either{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="True"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              /> or{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="False"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              />.
            </dd>
            <dt>Comparison Operator</dt>
            <dd>
              An operator like{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="=="
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              /> or{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code=">="
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              /> that compares two values and produces a boolean.
            </dd>
            <dt>if Statement</dt>
            <dd>
              Runs a block of code only when its condition is{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="True"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              />.
            </dd>
            <dt>Condition</dt>
            <dd>
              The boolean expression an{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="if"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              /> statement checks.
            </dd>
            <dt>Code Block</dt>
            <dd>
              A group of statements, marked in Python by indentation.
            </dd>
            <dt>Logical Operator</dt>
            <dd>
              <CodeSnippet
                code="and"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              />,{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="or"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              />, and{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="not"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              /> &mdash; combine or invert booleans.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">2.</span> Branching</h2>

          <p>
            An{" "}
            <CodeSnippet
              code="if"
              lang={"python"}
              theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
              inline
            /> can be extended into a chain. Only the first branch whose condition
            is true will run, and this is also where you first imported the{" "}
            <CodeSnippet
              code="random"
              lang={"python"}
              theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
              inline
            /> module.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>else</dt>
            <dd>
              Runs when every condition before it was{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="False"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              />.
            </dd>
            <dt>elif</dt>
            <dd>
              Chains another condition onto an{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="if"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              /> &mdash; only the first true branch runs.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">3.</span> Nesting</h2>

          <p>
            A conditional can live inside another conditional, which lets you
            ask a follow-up question only when the first answer was yes.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Nesting</dt>
            <dd>
              Placing one code block (like an{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="if"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              />) inside another.
            </dd>
            <dt>pass</dt>
            <dd>
              A placeholder statement that does nothing &mdash; used where
              Python requires a block but you have nothing to put there yet.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">4.</span> while Loops</h2>

          <p>
            A{" "}
            <CodeSnippet
              code="while"
              lang={"python"}
              theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
              inline
            /> loop repeats as long as its condition holds. Something inside the
            loop has to change that condition, or it never ends.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Iteration</dt>
            <dd>Repeating a block of code multiple times.</dd>
            <dt>while Loop</dt>
            <dd>
              Repeats its block as long as its condition is{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="True"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              />.
            </dd>
            <dt>Infinite Loop</dt>
            <dd>
              A loop whose condition never becomes{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="False"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              />, so it never stops.
            </dd>
            <dt>Sentinel Value</dt>
            <dd>A specific value a loop watches for to know when to stop.</dd>
            <dt>Built-in Function</dt>
            <dd>
              A function Python already provides, like{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="round()"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              /> &mdash; avoid naming variables the same thing.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">5.</span> for Loops</h2>

          <p>
            When you know how many times to repeat, a{" "}
            <CodeSnippet
              code="for"
              lang={"python"}
              theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
              inline
            /> loop is the better fit.{" "}
            <CodeSnippet
              code="range()"
              lang={"python"}
              theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
              inline
            /> supplies the numbers to count through.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>for Loop</dt>
            <dd>Repeats its block once for each value in a sequence.</dd>
            <dt>range()</dt>
            <dd>
              Generates a sequence of numbers for a{" "}
              <CodeSnippet
                code="for"
                lang={"python"}
                theme={"material-theme-ocean"}
                inline
              /> loop to count through.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">6.</span> Nested Loops</h2>

          <p>
            A loop inside a loop runs the inner block once for every combination
            &mdash; the inner loop finishes completely on each pass of the outer
            one.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Nested Loop</dt>
            <dd>A loop written inside the body of another loop.</dd>
            <dt>Outer Loop</dt>
            <dd>The loop that contains another loop inside it.</dd>
            <dt>Inner Loop</dt>
            <dd>
              The loop nested inside another &mdash; it completes fully for
              every pass of the outer loop.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  dl {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  dt {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  dd {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }
  section {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  code {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
</style>
